    {
      "id": "xcVOKjsGg2S9WKP3EdWoz",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 806.0544967133862,
      "y": 470.1684576742143,
      "width": 273.1521946256414,
      "height": 75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b23",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1866115411,
      "version": 446,
      "versionNonce": 1566124079,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791381514674,
      "created": 1791294675760,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The problem is that in\norder to store the data\nyou have to know its shape",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The problem is that in order to store the data you have to know its shape",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "lBoYh4cDDvW07GSk4ewrv",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 636.2324554352282,
      "y": -561.6491774585712,
      "width": 298.15302889964585,
      "height": 600,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b24",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 534347197,
      "version": 1022,
      "versionNonce": 1940356353,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791381530885,
      "created": 1791295440547,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Maybe this is too generic\n\nWe can classify what kind of\ndata we produce:\n\nif were doing a visual on\nconcentration we're producing\nxarray<double>[5]\n\nbut maybe we don't always\nwant all channels?\n\nmaybe even down sample in\nwhich case the type stays\nthe same\n\non the other hand we can\nproduce a scalar or scalars\nper channel so like\n[]. Even though technically\nxarray<double> can be an\narray with one element...\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Maybe this is too generic\n\nWe can classify what kind of data we produce:\n\nif were doing a visual on concentration we're producing\nxarray<double>[5]\n\nbut maybe we don't always want all channels?\n\nmaybe even down sample in which case the type stays the same\n\non the other hand we can produce a scalar or scalars per channel so like\n[]. Even though technically\nxarray<double> can be an array with one element...\n\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
